  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "The task here is five-fold:",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "1) Remove all karaf dependencies on fcrepo-camel-toolbox.  It is only necessary in this first round of updates to cover the services that are currently in highest demand:  fcrepo,fcrepo-indexing-solr and fcrepo-indexing-triplestore.",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "2) Upgrade camel to use the latest camel version (3.9.0)",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "3) Reorganize the camel toolbox so that it can be executed as a stand-alone Java 11 jar.",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "4) Add support for a -c <properties file path> in order to configure your camel microservices.",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "5) Add the ability to enable select services (such as Solr or triplestore indexing) via the properties file.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
